Cache extxyz in Orbax and train SpookyPhysNet with charge/spin inputs.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --extxyz EXTXYZ       Input extxyz file, e.g. so3lr_train.extxyz. Required
                        for --mode cache/cache-and-train (used to derive the
                        cache path). Not needed for --mode train if --cache-
                        path is given directly.
  --cache-dir CACHE_DIR
                        Directory for Orbax data caches
  --cache-path CACHE_PATH
                        Exact path to a pre-built Orbax data cache to train
                        from (e.g. one produced by
                        split_and_inspect_ml_mm_dataset.py's train_cache/).
                        Bypasses the --extxyz/--cache-dir hash-based lookup.
                        Only valid with --mode train.
  --workdir WORKDIR     Training output/checkpoint directory
  --mode {cache,train,cache-and-train}
  --force-recache       Overwrite existing matching data cache
  --energy-key ENERGY_KEY
                        ASE info key for scalar energy target
  --forces-key FORCES_KEY
                        ASE arrays key for force target
  --dipole-key DIPOLE_KEY
                        ASE info key for dipole target
  --charge-key CHARGE_KEY
                        ASE info key for total molecular charge
  --spin-key SPIN_KEY   ASE info key for spin multiplicity; defaults to
                        singlet
  --default-charge DEFAULT_CHARGE
  --default-spin DEFAULT_SPIN
  --no-infer-spin       Use --default-spin when --spin-key is absent instead
                        of electron parity
  --max-structures MAX_STRUCTURES
                        Optional smoke-test cap
  --valid-fraction VALID_FRACTION
  --num-devices NUM_DEVICES
  --batch-size-per-device BATCH_SIZE_PER_DEVICE
  --max-pairs-per-device MAX_PAIRS_PER_DEVICE
                        Approximate per-device batch*n_atoms^2 budget;
                        automatically reduces the structure batch for larger
                        molecules
  --epochs EPOCHS
  --restart RESTART     Path to an epoch-* checkpoint, or 'latest' to use the
                        newest under --workdir
  --init-checkpoint INIT_CHECKPOINT
                        Warm-start compatible parameters from a checkpoint
                        while initializing new heads and optimizer state from
                        scratch
  --auto-resume         Resume from newest epoch-* under --workdir when
                        present
  --steps-per-epoch STEPS_PER_EPOCH
  --valid-steps VALID_STEPS
  --save-every SAVE_EVERY
                        Save a checkpoint every N epochs.
  --save-every-steps SAVE_EVERY_STEPS
                        Additionally save a mid-epoch checkpoint every N
                        optimizer steps (global step count, across epochs). 0
                        disables this (default).
  --optimizer {adamw,muon}
                        Optimizer for 2D+ weight matrices. 'muon'
                        orthogonalizes matrix updates via Newton-Schulz and
                        routes non-matrix params (biases, embeddings) through
                        AdamW internally. Muon's opt_state is not compatible
                        with an AdamW checkpoint's opt_state; use --init-
                        checkpoint (not --restart) to warm-start params only
                        when switching optimizers.
  --muon-beta MUON_BETA
                        Muon momentum decay
  --muon-adam-lr MUON_ADAM_LR
                        Learning rate for Muon's internal AdamW branch (non-
                        matrix params); defaults to --learning-rate
  --muon-adam-b1 MUON_ADAM_B1
  --muon-adam-b2 MUON_ADAM_B2
  --learning-rate LEARNING_RATE
  --lr-schedule {constant,warmup_cosine}
                        Optimizer LR schedule (default: linear warmup followed
                        by cosine decay).
  --lr-warmup-steps LR_WARMUP_STEPS
                        Linear warmup steps for --lr-schedule warmup_cosine
                        (default: 1000).
  --lr-decay-steps LR_DECAY_STEPS
                        Cosine-decay horizon; 0 derives it from epochs and
                        train batches.
  --lr-end-fraction LR_END_FRACTION
                        Final LR divided by peak LR for cosine decay (default:
                        0.05).
  --weight-decay WEIGHT_DECAY
  --clip-global-norm CLIP_GLOBAL_NORM
  --energy-weight ENERGY_WEIGHT
  --forces-weight FORCES_WEIGHT
  --dipole-weight DIPOLE_WEIGHT
  --charges-weight CHARGES_WEIGHT
  --mbd-checkpoint MBD_CHECKPOINT
                        Frozen QCML MBD checkpoint. Its energy/forces are
                        added to Spooky's prediction, so Spooky trains the
                        remaining residual.
  --no-cgenff-vdw       Disable the empirical CGenFF Lennard-Jones term even
                        if cgenff_master_sigmas/epsilons/cgenff_type_idx are
                        present in the cache. Useful when training with --mbd-
                        checkpoint instead of empirical LJ dispersion, to
                        avoid double-counting dispersion physics between the
                        two. mol_id-based electrostatics masking is
                        unaffected.
  --mbd-weight MBD_WEIGHT
                        Scale for the frozen MBD energy and forces (default:
                        1.0).
  --mbd-ramp-steps MBD_RAMP_STEPS
                        Linearly introduce the frozen MBD correction over this
                        many optimizer steps (default: 10000; 0 enables it
                        immediately).
  --multipole-checkpoint MULTIPOLE_CHECKPOINT
                        Frozen QCML multipole model checkpoint (Orbax dir or
                        portable JSON). Its predicted molecular dipole is used
                        as an auxiliary consistency target for the network's
                        own learned-charge dipole, on top of the DFT-reference
                        dipole loss (see --multipole-consistency-weight).
  --multipole-consistency-weight MULTIPOLE_CONSISTENCY_WEIGHT
                        Weight for the MSE between the network's learned-
                        charge dipole and the frozen multipole model's
                        predicted dipole (default: 1.0; only used when
                        --multipole-checkpoint is set).
  --features FEATURES
  --max-degree MAX_DEGREE
  --num-iterations NUM_ITERATIONS
  --num-basis-functions NUM_BASIS_FUNCTIONS
  --cutoff CUTOFF
  --max-atomic-number MAX_ATOMIC_NUMBER
